#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:5
msgid "Tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:7
msgid ""
"This tutorial sets up two ANet nodes on one machine and completes a paid "
"capability call between them. One node, the *provider*, publishes a small"
" text-digest service and charges 2 credits per call. The other node, the "
"*requester*, discovers the service, pays for a call and checks the "
"result, the receipt and the spending."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:13
msgid "The tutorial covers these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:15
msgid ":ref:`Create two identities <intro-tutorial-identities>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:16
msgid ":ref:`Register both nodes with a hub <intro-tutorial-register>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:17
msgid ""
":ref:`Write the service and publish it as a capability <intro-tutorial-"
"publish>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:19
msgid ":ref:`Find the capability and read its card <intro-tutorial-find>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:20
msgid ":ref:`Call it and confirm the first payment <intro-tutorial-call>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:21
msgid ":ref:`Allow automatic payment for a known provider <intro-tutorial-auto>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:23
msgid ":ref:`Inspect the result and verify the receipt <intro-tutorial-result>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:25
msgid ":ref:`Read the delivery state <intro-tutorial-delivery>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:26
msgid ":ref:`Review the spending <intro-tutorial-spend>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:30
msgid "On this page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:35
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:37
msgid ""
"``anet`` is installed as described in :doc:`install`, and ``anet doctor``"
" reports no failed check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:39
msgid ""
"A hub is available. The examples use ``https://hub.example.com``. Replace"
" it with the address of the hub in use. Two points about the hub matter "
"for this tutorial:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:43
msgid ""
"If the hub admits by AID, its operator has to run one command per node, "
"``anet-hub admit``. The operator can attach a starting balance with "
"``--grant``. The requester needs credit to pay for the call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:46
msgid ""
"If the hub has open registration, the admission step does not appear. A "
"new account is on probation for 72 hours and receives the trial credit "
"only when the probation has ended. The requester then cannot pay in this "
"tutorial until that time has passed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:51
msgid "``python3`` is available for the sample service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:53
msgid ""
"Both nodes run on one machine. Each has its own identity, data directory "
"and control port. To run the nodes on two machines instead, install "
"``anet`` on both, leave out the ``--id`` option from every command and "
"run the commands of each role on its own machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:61
msgid "Create two identities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:63
msgid ""
"``anet id new`` creates a named identity with its own data directory "
"under ``~/.anet/ids`` and starts a daemon for it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:77
msgid ""
"Each command ends with the status of the new node. The hub state is "
"``none`` because no hub has been joined yet. The listing shows both "
"identities and the control port of each:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:88
msgid ""
"``anet --id NAME COMMAND`` runs any command for one identity. The AID of "
"each node is printed by ``anet status``. The following commands store the"
" two AIDs in shell variables for the rest of the tutorial:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:102
msgid "Register both nodes with a hub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:104
msgid ""
"``anet hub-register`` adds the identity to a hub. The daemon submits the "
"key event log and the set of encryption keys, and the hub verifies that "
"the node controls the identity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:116
msgid ""
"On a hub that admits by AID, the last line is the command for the "
"operator. Registration is retried in the background and completes within "
"a short time after the operator has run that command. The requester is "
"registered in the same way:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:125
msgid ""
"The operator of the hub now admits both AIDs and attaches the starting "
"balance to the requester. The commands run on the hub host, with "
"``--data`` naming the data directory of the hub when it is not the "
"working directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:137
msgid "Wait until both nodes report the state ``registered``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:146
msgid "Recovery passphrase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:148
msgid ""
"The warning in the output of ``hub-register`` has a cause. When the "
"command runs in a terminal, it asks for a recovery passphrase on the "
"first registration and writes an encrypted recovery file. The passphrase "
"is entered on the terminal only; the daemon never reads it. It is "
"required to rotate keys, to move the identity to another hub and to "
"restore it on another machine, and ANet cannot recover it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:155
msgid ""
"When no terminal is available, as when a coding agent runs the command, "
"registration still completes and the identity is usable at once. The "
"recovery seed is then protected only by a key inside the data directory, "
"the identity state is *unprotected*, and ``anet status`` and ``anet "
"doctor`` repeat the warning. ``anet identity protect``, run on a "
"terminal, sets the passphrase and replaces the recovery seed. Seeds that "
"were copied before that point become invalid. Until then, a leak of the "
"data directory can allow the identity to be taken over. For the states "
"and the commands, see :doc:`/topics/identity`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:170
msgid "Write the service and publish it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:172
msgid ""
"A capability is a name that other nodes can call and a local service that"
" answers. The service module connects the two: the daemon sends the call "
"arguments as a JSON object in an HTTP ``POST`` and expects a JSON object "
"in return. The service needs no knowledge of ANet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:177
msgid ""
"The service in this tutorial returns the SHA-256 digest of a text. It "
"listens on a Unix domain socket, which is the recommended form: the "
"daemon checks, before it writes anything to the socket, that the path can"
" be changed only by trusted accounts and that the listening process runs "
"as the owner of the socket."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:183
msgid "Save the following as ``digest_service.py``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:224
msgid ""
"Start it in a separate terminal and call it directly once to confirm that"
" it works:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:234
msgid "Publishing needs two entries in the configuration of the provider:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:236
msgid "``modules.service.capabilities``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:237
msgid ""
"Declares the capability: its identifier, the URL of the service, the "
"price in credits and a description. A price of ``0`` or no price means "
"the capability is free."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:241
msgid "``inbound.public_capabilities``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:242
msgid ""
"Lists the capability identifiers that callers outside the peer lists may "
"call. A capability that is declared but not listed here does not appear "
"on the public card."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:246
msgid ""
"The following command adds both entries to the configuration of the "
"provider. It reads the existing file, so the other keys remain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:269
msgid ""
"``anet doctor`` confirms that the service is reachable and that the "
"capability is public:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:279
msgid ""
"The inbound policy remains ``closed``. The policy governs free-form tasks"
" from unlisted peers; the public capability is the only thing the node "
"offers to them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:286
msgid "Find the capability and read its card"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:288
msgid ""
"The requester lists the agents on the hub. The query text, if one is "
"given, is matched on the requesting node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:297
msgid ""
"The column ``charge`` is ``free``, ``partial`` or ``paid``. It is derived"
" from the a2a-x402 declaration on the public card, without contacting the"
" provider. ``key`` shows whether the hub has confirmed the current key of"
" the agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:302
msgid ""
"``anet card`` shows the card with the prices. The provider signs the "
"prices, and the requester's node obtains them end to end, so the hub "
"never holds them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:316
msgid "Call the capability and confirm the first payment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:318
msgid ""
"The requester sends the call. A priced capability answers with a quote "
"instead of a result, and a new node pays nothing automatically, so the "
"call stops at the quote:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:346
msgid ""
"The task is an A2A task. It is in the state ``input-required``, and the "
"metadata ``x402.payment.status`` is ``payment-required``, as the a2a-x402"
" extension specifies. The reason ``needs_operator_approval`` means that "
"the decision belongs to the operator. The ``payment`` line states what "
"was quoted, the limit that applied and the next command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:352
msgid ""
"``anet pay`` is the confirmation. It runs on a terminal, prints the quote"
" and the limit that applies to a confirmed payment, and signs the "
"authorization only after the answer ``yes``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:372
msgid ""
"The authorization is valid for this task only. The provider checks the "
"payee, the amount, the binding to the task and the expiry, asks the hub "
"to settle it, and executes the capability after the settlement. Agents "
"that act through MCP or the local A2A interface cannot confirm the "
"payment on behalf of the operator: their payments are limited by "
"``agent_max`` and ``agent_daily_max``, which are ``0`` initially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:379
msgid ""
"A quote that exceeds the price on the provider's signed card is never "
"paid automatically, and the sentence in the task states the difference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:387
msgid "Allow automatic payment for a known provider"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:389
msgid ""
"Automatic payment needs two settings, both made on a terminal and both "
"asking for confirmation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:392
msgid "the provider is added to the payee list, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:393
msgid "the limit for one automatic payment, ``auto_max``, is raised above ``0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:405
msgid ""
"Each change is recorded in the evidence chain of the node. ``anet "
"payments`` prints the limits and the amounts spent today."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:408
msgid "The next call is paid without further input:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:417
msgid ""
"The task needs a few seconds for the quote, the settlement and the "
"execution. If ``task get`` shows the state ``TASK_STATE_WORKING``, repeat"
" it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:423
msgid "Inspect the result and verify the receipt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:425
msgid ""
"``anet task get`` prints the complete task. The result is the artifact "
"named ``anet.result``; the payment is in the metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:472
msgid "Three fields establish what happened:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:474
msgid "``evidence.observed_state``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:475
msgid ""
"The answer of the service. ``verify_trust: 1`` records that the service "
"answered and nothing more. The node cannot establish whether the answer "
"is correct, and no configuration of the provider can claim more unless "
"the service itself returns an ``evidence`` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:480
msgid "``anet.receipt_verified``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:481
msgid ""
"The result is accompanied by a receipt that the provider signed. The "
"requester's node accepted the result only after the receipt matched the "
"request, the result and both identities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:485
msgid "``x402.payment.receipts``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:486
msgid ""
"The settlement receipt signed by the hub. The node records the payment as"
" settled only after it has checked that the authorization belongs to this"
" task, that the payee is the provider and that the amount matches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:490
msgid "``anet verify`` repeats the receipt check later, from the stored data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:506
msgid ""
"The same check works on a different machine with no daemon, hub or "
"network, given the receipt and the key history of the provider, which are"
" the fields ``anet.receipt.receipt`` and ``anet.receipt.provider_kel`` of"
" the task metadata:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:525
msgid "Read the delivery state"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:527
msgid ""
"A signed result states that the provider produced it. The delivery state "
"states whether a message reached the other node. Each message the node "
"sends has one of three states:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:535
msgid "``anet.delivery``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:536
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:537
msgid "``pending``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:538
msgid ""
"The message is on its way. ``anet.delivery_detail`` says where it is: "
"``not_sent`` (the node could not reach the hub and retries), ``sent`` "
"(handed to the hub, not yet confirmed) or ``queued_at_hub`` (stored at "
"the hub until the other node collects it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:543
msgid "``confirmed``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:544
msgid ""
"The other node has opened the message and confirmed it. The sentence "
"reads: \"Delivered: the other side's node confirmed it.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:546
msgid "``unconfirmed``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:547
msgid ""
"The node stopped waiting. With the detail ``not_sent`` the message never "
"left the node. With the detail ``sent`` it may still have arrived."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:551
msgid ""
"The confirmation is created by the receiving node. The hub keeps the "
"status of a message for 7 days, and the sender asks for it with a random "
"identifier. While a message is pending, the sentence ends with the time "
"at which the task fails if the message is still not delivered. That time "
"is the earlier of two moments: ``no_response_after`` (15 minutes by "
"default) after the message was handed over, and the end of the message "
"lifetime of 14 days."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:559
msgid ""
"If delivery is not confirmed within the limit, the task fails with the "
"reason code ``delivery_unconfirmed`` and the node asks the other side to "
"cancel it, so that a request the sender has abandoned is not executed "
"after the other node comes online. The sentence states the variant that "
"applies, for example \"Delivery was not confirmed within <limit>: it is "
"still waiting at the hub (the other side may be offline), and anet asked "
"them to cancel it; send it again later if you still need it.\" The "
"reference lists all variants under :ref:`reason codes <reference-reason-"
"codes>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:568
msgid ""
"The state is part of the task projection in the CLI, in the MCP tools "
"``get_task`` and ``wait_task``, and on the local A2A interface. A task "
"that has reached a final state no longer carries the closing sentence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:577
msgid "Review the spending"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:579
msgid "Three commands show the requester's side:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:608
msgid ""
"The daily total counts the authorizations that were signed, not the "
"amounts that were settled. In a ledger entry, the reason of a payment is "
"the identifier of its authorization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:612
msgid "The provider's balance has increased by the same amount:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:619
msgid ""
"The evidence chain records each step, signed by the node that took it. "
"The filter ``--type`` selects an event type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../intro/tutorial.rst:634
msgid ""
"``anet audit --export DIR`` writes the whole chain with the key history, "
"and ``anet verify --chain DIR`` checks it elsewhere. The reconciliation "
"commands ``anet reconcile`` and ``anet audit-hub`` compare the node's "
"payment record and balance proof with the ledger and the issuance chain "
"of the hub. They are described in :doc:`/topics/payments`."
msgstr ""

